<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01Q2">Example <span data-tag="01Q2">6.3.0.3</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{Kan}$ denote the category of Kan complexes and let $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ denote the homotopy category of Kan complexes (Construction <a data-tag="00TY" href="/tag/00TY">3.1.5.10</a>). Then the quotient functor $\operatorname{Kan}\rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ exhibits $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Kan}}$ as a strict localization of $\operatorname{Kan}$ with respect to the collection of all homotopy equivalences (see Corollary <a data-tag="012V" href="/tag/012V">3.1.8.7</a>). </p>
